        "original_id": "ed0437eb-f975-5c0e-81b3-ada0706954aa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Singapore\n- Buildings: Tanjong Pagar Centre, One Raffles Place, UOB Plaza, Republic Plaza, 63 Building, Bank of China Tower\n- Topics: tallest buildings, building height records\n\nFacts:\n- In 1986, One Raffles Place was completed at 280 m and became the tallest building in the world outside North America, surpassing South Korea's 63 Building.\n- One Raffles Place remained the tallest building in the world outside North America until Bank of China Tower succeeded it.\n- UOB Plaza, One Raffles Place, and Republic Plaza jointly held Singapore's tallest-building record for over 20 years.\n- Tanjong Pagar Centre is 290 m tall.\n- Tanjong Pagar Centre currently holds the title of tallest building in Singapore.\n- Tanjong Pagar Centre broke the previous Singapore height record jointly held by UOB Plaza, One Raffles Place, and Republic Plaza.",
